.TH KAGI-VOLUME-ISCSI-EXPORT 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-volume-iscsi-export \- export an attached Kagi block device with Linux LIO
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/kagi-volume-iscsi-export
.I /dev/nbdN IQN PORTAL-IP
.RI [ LUN ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Use this helper after attaching a Kagi volume to a Linux NBD device.
With
.BR targetcli ,
it creates an LIO block backstore and an iSCSI target, adds the device at
the requested LUN, attempts to configure the portal on port 3260, and
saves the target configuration.
The default LUN number is 0.
The helper needs permission to modify the kernel target configuration.
.PP
Verify the active portal, initiator ACLs, and authentication before exposing
the target to initiators.
Raft remains the authority for Kagi persistent reservations.
Use a reservation-aware SCSI bridge when initiators must send persistent
reservation commands to Kagi.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kagi-volume-attach (1),
.BR kagi-volume-nbd (1),
.BR targetcli (8)
